{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1504195-kuei-jin-the-hungry-ghost","id":1504195,"title":"Kuei Jin: The Hungry Ghost","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-02T03:19:11-08:00","id":1504195,"title":"Kuei Jin: The Hungry Ghost","content":"Hello all, Im the writer of the V5 Kuei Jin: The Hungry Ghost. <br /> <br /> Overall there has been many good responses to the work. Ultimately this post is for any of you out there who downloaded the pdf and me wanting to know your thoughts, opinions and questions if there is any!<br /> <br /> For those that don\u2019t know it exists, its a V5 expansion to playing the Kuei Jin and it is Pay what you Want!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/426440/Kuei-Jin-The-Hungry-Ghosts?affiliate_id=3794988\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/images/1/426440.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/426440/Kuei-Jin-The-Hungry-Ghosts?affiliate_id=3794988\" target=\"_blank\"> Kuei Jin: The Hungry Ghosts - White Wolf | Storytellers Vault </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/426440/Kuei-Jin-The-Hungry-Ghosts?affiliate_id=3794988\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/426440/Kuei-Jin-The-Hungry-Ghosts?affiliate_id=3794988 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Kuei Jin: The Hungry Ghosts - The Great Departure had come and gone. The Kindred of the East has seemingly disappeared, leaving only memories. However </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27804-studiokohvi","name":"Studiokohvi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27804_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T14:36:08-08:00","id":1504225,"title":"","content":"How long did the project take? <br /> <br /> Did you work on this alone or with a team?<br /> <br /> Did you tell anyone about it while you were working on it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T16:42:24-08:00","id":1504229,"title":"","content":"1) The project took about a year and a several months of work.<br /> <br /> 2) With a team.<br /> <br /> 3) Ive told some friends and family members but in terms of online presence, there was none.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27804-studiokohvi","name":"Studiokohvi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27804_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T18:02:53-08:00","id":1504233,"title":"","content":"Did you ever get any pushback? Did anyone ask why you wanted to do this or say if they thought it was a bad idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T01:06:48-08:00","id":1504248,"title":"","content":"Hmmm \ud83e\udd14 There wasn\u2019t any pushback as most people who knew about the Kuei Jin understood there were portrayal problems with the books itself.<br /> <br /> My friends did ask why I wanted to do this. My answer to them and yourself is the same. KotE mechanically and core ideas have a lot of merit. I don't appreciate that all the vampires in the world essentially started around cainites especially the geographic distance each one had to travel to most of Asia with which V5 is dancing around the issue. However, I understand Paradox\u2019s hesitancy with it but the fact that places such as Singapore still run the original kuei jin mechanics (lore wise they just cut out bits that is just excessive) shows that there is a lot of love for these creatures and imv should not be abandoned.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27804-studiokohvi","name":"Studiokohvi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27804_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T18:53:08-08:00","id":1504310,"title":"","content":"I really think you made a great effort at this, and the book looks amazingly professional. Character sheet is so well made I want to play with it.<br /> The artist was especially well chosen and evokes the strong inks of the original.<br /> Really, great work.<br /> <br /> I appreciate the effort to make it more neutral, but I would have loved a take that's more personalized towards local cultures where the Hungry Ghosts appear.<br /> <br /> Did you look into any other KotE revival projects while doing this?<br /> What motivated you to work this into V5?<br /> What made you settle on the terms that you did and the disciplines that you did?<br /> Are you concerned that any formal attempt at Wraith 5 may trash a lot of the work you did here?<br /> What made you simplify the travel to the spirit worlds?<br /> How do you see the Hengeyokai interacting with these Hungry Ghosts? I've noticed you only mentioned &quot;Lupines&quot;<br /> How do you see the Kindred interacting with the Hungry Ghosts? How was the history of the world affected by this version?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-04T09:38:06-08:00","id":1504370,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> Thank you very much for you kind comments! My close friends and I poured a bit of ourselves into this work and we all really appreciate how well received it looks visually. When I saw his work on layout and designs, I was worried that the writing wouldn\u2019t be up to par!<br /> <br /> The artist is a kind and brilliant illustrator who has his pedigree in comics. He is a fan of the Kuei Jin and it shows!<br /> <br /> In terms of making it more localised, when we all had some time to rest, I plan to have an expansion such as more paths and schools including my thoughts on how the courts have transitioned in v5. Also likely a template to have a how to create your own courts \ud83d\ude05<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Whilst doing the work, I didn\u2019t. However I found after completing the writing that Hsienfan is doing essentially a K20 anniversary edition using V20 ruleset. They do great work in which I can recommend.</li> <li>V5 is how I got into Vampires and WoD in general. In that sense Im more attuned to it thematically and mechanically. As a result, I just wanted to play a kuei jin using V5 rules \ud83d\ude05</li> <li>Translation can be difficult but the main reason why I went for more neutral terms is in KotE, it heavily implies to me that other KJ uses the same terms such as mandarin, Xue or otherwise. Now that probably isint in the case in universe (hopefully not) but subtly to me anyway, it makes it seem as if Asia is one big homogenous culture that uses the exact same terms. My aim is that its neutral and personable enough that everywhere in the world, they can translate it to something they can understand. Hence the shift of terms from KJ to Hungry Ghost, my Brazilian friends could easily translate that to \u2018Fantasmas Faminto\u2019 and from my understanding, everywhere in the world have their names for that. In terms of Disciplines, its based on both the Indo-European ideas of the elements and the Five phases which Chinese culture have influenced around their neighbours to be adopted. It stands to me that the Indian or European HG wont understand elements based around the five phases (unless educated into it) so I went to expand it out to include all of it.</li> <li>To be honest, no. V5 Cult of the Blood Gods is an excellent expansion and imv, seems to head a good direction on what Wraith should be like. Thinking about it now, that doesn\u2019t mean that the Wraith 5 team will take that into account but I hope it does. Hopefully they will keep wraith as it is and not similar to Geist. However, if it does in a completely different direction, then ultimately may think on updating the document to suit.</li> <li>Both in keeping the philosophy of V5 which is to be more rules light and thematically where the HG are now spiritually more powerful in that sense. The original document was far more crunchy but when reading through, it may fit V20 but didn\u2019t seem to fit V5. Also a personal gripe of mine is that I had to reread how to travel between spirit realms so many times (including reading werewolf 20 to understand the gist) that I just felt that as a player myself, I wouldnt want to go through it.</li> <li>Since W5 is not related to the old Werewolves, I dont quite know now how the beast courts will function. However, old lore wise, the Hengeyokai are far more advanced in the art of peace and war between themselves and the HG. They both cover different niches, both spirit travel and there isint a sense of straight up antagonism imv.</li> <li>Neonates and freshly embraced are gonna be confused. Probably thinking some obscure clan. The older generations who encountered the HG before their mass disappearance are going to have a sense of whiplash. The camarilla princes are likely to strike a deals with them again. The Barons most likely are divided on these issues and the Sabbat pack priests are going to be either friendly or antagonistic depending on their chosen Path. The old lore that KoTe had accrued hasn\u2019t changed or just been tweaked imv. Majority of it is kept intact. However, post 2004 is all the new lore is in how all the Courts have changed or collapsed due to huge population decline but individually, those that are left have been empowered.</li> </ol><br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27804-studiokohvi","name":"Studiokohvi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27804_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T10:13:27-08:00","id":1504606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Studiokohvi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1504195-kuei-jin-the-hungry-ghost?p=1504370#post1504370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However I found after completing the writing that Hsienfan is doing essentially a K20 anniversary edition using V20 ruleset. They do great work in which I can recommend.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you happen to have a link to that handy? I'd like to take a look because I was planning to do something simular in my own game and if I can save on work that would be great!\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T02:07:18-08:00","id":1504737,"title":"","content":"Here is Hsienfan forum for basically their interpretation.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/rehabilitating-kindred-of-the-east.867814/\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?thre...e-east.867814/</a><br /> <br /> Hsienfan Storyteller Vault stuff<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/341889/Analects-of-the-Damned\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/images/1/341889.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/341889/Analects-of-the-Damned\" target=\"_blank\"> Analects of the Damned - White Wolf | Storytellers Vault </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/341889/Analects-of-the-Damned\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/341889/Analects-of-the-Damned </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Analects of the Damned - Revisit the Game of Blood and Enlightenment In 1998, White Wolf Games released Kindred of the East, the flagship supplem </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27804-studiokohvi","name":"Studiokohvi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27804_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T03:53:47-08:00","id":1504745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Studiokohvi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1504195-kuei-jin-the-hungry-ghost?p=1504737#post1504737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is Hsienfan forum for basically their interpretation.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/rehabilitating-kindred-of-the-east.867814/\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?thre...e-east.867814/</a><br /> <br /> Hsienfan Storyteller Vault stuff<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/341889/Analects-of-the-Damned\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.storytellersvault.com/pr...-of-the-Damned</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I never quite understood what is supposed to be wrong with the original Kote . I don't have a degree in east asian history so i'd really like to know","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-10T01:50:49-08:00","id":1505012,"title":"","content":"Hmm, you don\u2019t particularly need a degree in east asian history to get a feel on why KoTE felt wrong. If anything, to have a basic understanding on why KotE feels incorrect is actually more a focus on the era of western imperialism, american pov of WW2 and the rise of popularity of martial arts films + anime in the west. The reason I say that is because when you\u2019re reading KotE and looking at the art, that feels as if thats what you\u2019re experiencing.<br /> <br /> <br /> TLDR<br /> <br /> -China is not the whole of Asia. Its part of Asia. Way its written is Asia is Chinese.<br /> <br /> -Japanese are not Chinese.<br /> <br /> -Some art used could be used as western WW2 propaganda<br /> <br /> -Martial arts is not a definitive defining feature of Asia<br /> <br /> -Anime + Manga isn\u2019t always the most accurate bar of depiction.<br /> <br /> Form the onset, KotE focuses on the middle kingdom which is basically china. But then the Kuei Jin in the original book also says the keui jin aren\u2019t just chinese but also expands to places like India, Myanmar, Malaysia and Philippines as an example. By the depiction and writing, it makes it seem that all of the above places are Chinese which is obviously not true. Another thing is whilst talking about the middle kingdom, also uses a lot of Japanese terms mixed in.<br /> <br /> <br /> The book itself basically merges Japanese and Chinese culture together. From a outsiders pov, I can understand the similarities as Japan is a cultural heir and a form of a capsule for Tang dynasty China especially when the Taika reforms around 645 Ad were introduced. Chinese culture and ruling system from that era was adopted and adapted to fit Japan. As a tangent, chinese culture changed significantly depending on the dynasty that controlled China so when there is exchanges between Japan and China in the ancient past, China viewed Japan simply as old fashioned when Tang dynasty was destroyed and a new dynasty was established. If you look up the art styles, clothes and other cultural stuff on the internet alone, you can see where the major similarities started. However, Japanese culture is unique as there has been so much adaption over 1300+ years that its severely unfair to say they are a copy. A modern example is as if saying American culture is the exact same as British culture. There are many overt similarities but its unfair to say they are the same.<br /> <br /> <br /> A lot of the art in the original KotE basically was Yellow peril at its finest. This was particularly common in how chinese + Japanese were depicted by western countries during the end of imperialism and was majorly revived in during WW2. Its an obvious caricature of East Asian but considering how much historical hurt that it has caused to Asian expats, this one is quite a sore spot.<br /> <br /> \u200b<img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1172_1678441654681_441\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1172\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1172\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1172&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/>\u200b<br /> <br /> <img title=\"image.jpg\" data-tempid=\"temp_1173_1678441842688_408\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1173\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1173\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1173&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/>\u200b<br /> <br /> A major thing when playing KotE is as well a focus on martial arts. Now most of the world have their own traditions of martial arts (western boxing is a martial art imv) so why is this particularly heightened in KotE as a own separate skill? The obvious influence when reading through is clearly Hong Kong martial art films which the writers must have enjoyed. However, there is already a brawl skill there. Martial arts is a form of that or melee if you use hand weapons.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anime + Manga can be an insight into the culture itself but it depends on what type from the 80s + 90s. Imagine a person only basing their entire views of peoples culture just on action comic books from the 90s and then expecting that to be it.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27804-studiokohvi","name":"Studiokohvi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27804_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-10T09:13:16-08:00","id":1505020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Studiokohvi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1504195-kuei-jin-the-hungry-ghost?p=1505012#post1505012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A major thing when playing KotE is as well a focus on martial arts. Now most of the world have their own traditions of martial arts (western boxing is a martial art imv) so why is this particularly heightened in KotE as a own separate skill? The obvious influence when reading through is clearly Hong Kong martial art films which the writers must have enjoyed. However, there is already a brawl skill there. Martial arts is a form of that or melee if you use hand weapons.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything else you said is correct, however the martial arts subsystem is neither a major feature of KotE (it takes up less than 1% if the page count in the core and is not elaborated in the supplements) nor is it kote specific - it's a truncated relic of two separate white wolf books - Street Fighter and WoD: Combat that tried to make the combat crunchier and more flavourful with mixed success to say the least. Mage has the same subsystems with Do since the beginning and keeps it in M20.<br /> <br /> In general KotE gets better with the supplements as they create a distinction between courts on local, cultural and religious differences, and that the core was mostly the Quincux perspective. Sadly, for many their exploration ends with the cringe of whitey must die and the utterly unnecesarry terminology salad.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-10T09:51:33-08:00","id":1505023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1504195-kuei-jin-the-hungry-ghost?p=1504745#post1504745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never quite understood what is supposed to be wrong with the original Kote . I don't have a degree in east asian history so i'd really like to know</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a podcast about the original KotE, hosted by three Canadians (I think they're all Canadians) of various Asian ancestries. It is just over two hours, and I can tell you that about an hour in, so halfway through, they made it to page <i>seven</i>. Not a hundred pages in, not fifty pages, <i>SEVEN</i> pages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/nKic0LVGfC4\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/nKic0LVGfC4\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/nKic0LVGfC4\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/nKic0LVGfC4 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I knew when I first got the book it was at least a little bit problematic, with the way they talk about how &quot;the West had never penetrated into the Orient,&quot; (because well, they did, there were a few wars that resulted), and the way the Kuei-Jin's arrival into the West was always portrayed as &quot;an invasion&quot; rather than &quot;a diaspora.&quot; But even I didn't expect the first seven pages to take a whole hour. That alone should give you a vague idea of what might be wrong. <br /> <br /> I'm not trying to rag on KotE, I have the original handbook, a pdf of one Dharma and a physical copy of another. But old White Wolf was like an angry bull in a porcelain shop, and half of what I hear and read about V5 seems to be redressing or retconning insensitive things written in previous editions (the other half seems to be almost complaints about the retconning and redressing). <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-10T11:07:47-08:00","id":1505026,"title":"","content":"In addition to what's been said already it's also a two-sided attack because there's also VtM fans who disliked the Kindred of the East getting retconned into a different species of vampire rather than Cainites who inhabit a different culture (I've had a peripheral interest in the Kuei-Jin due to the Exalted connection).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-11T08:42:48-08:00","id":1505118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1504195-kuei-jin-the-hungry-ghost?p=1505020#post1505020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everything else you said is correct, however the martial arts subsystem is neither a major feature of KotE (it takes up less than 1% if the page count in the core and is not elaborated in the supplements) nor is it kote specific - it's a truncated relic of two separate white wolf books - Street Fighter and WoD: Combat that tried to make the combat crunchier and more flavourful with mixed success to say the least. Mage has the same subsystems with Do since the beginning and keeps it in M20.<br /> <br /> In general KotE gets better with the supplements as they create a distinction between courts on local, cultural and religious differences, and that the core was mostly the Quincux perspective. Sadly, for many their exploration ends with the cringe of whitey must die and the utterly unnecesarry terminology salad.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah thats my bad then. Whilst Im intrigued by the lore pf mage, I have yet to play M20. Consider this my ignorance on the matter<br /> <br /> I agree on that the expansions are much better and imv Blood and Silk was their best one though most dark ages work were awesome most of the time anyway.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27804-studiokohvi","name":"Studiokohvi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27804_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-11T08:48:57-08:00","id":1505119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1504195-kuei-jin-the-hungry-ghost?p=1505026#post1505026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition to what's been said already it's also a two-sided attack because there's also VtM fans who disliked the Kindred of the East getting retconned into a different species of vampire rather than Cainites who inhabit a different culture (I've had a peripheral interest in the Kuei-Jin due to the Exalted connection).</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a split issue with the community. Its quite obvious what my stance is but there are those that wish the Kuei Jin were just cainites. To me it seems a waste and the ties to Exalted with one of their potential fates of reality turning into the World of Darkness is cool (even if the official line doesn't want to admit there may be an alternate reality connection outright).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27804-studiokohvi","name":"Studiokohvi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27804_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T04:34:55-07:00","id":1506132,"title":"","content":"Hello people,<br /> <br /> Thanks to all the support, we are in copper best seller!<br /> <br /> In the future, Im planning to have an expansion mainly focusing on the lore that I have written for in the V5 paradigm. Whilst I have a general idea on what Im going to do for the pre 2004 courts in modern times such as Golden Courts, Green courts etc, it isint set in stone and Im open to ideas if any of you would like to have some input.<br /> <br /> So the question I want to ask is what in your own table or head cannon has happened to the courts post the Great Departure? Have they changed or rebranded? Destroyed outright? <br /> <br /> I would be interested to read through all of your thoughts and ideas!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27804-studiokohvi","name":"Studiokohvi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27804_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T22:10:38-07:00","id":1506211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Studiokohvi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1504195-kuei-jin-the-hungry-ghost?p=1506132#post1506132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello people,<br /> <br /> Thanks to all the support, we are in copper best seller!<br /> <br /> In the future, Im planning to have an expansion mainly focusing on the lore that I have written for in the V5 paradigm. Whilst I have a general idea on what Im going to do for the pre 2004 courts in modern times such as Golden Courts, Green courts etc, it isint set in stone and Im open to ideas if any of you would like to have some input.<br /> <br /> So the question I want to ask is what in your own table or head cannon has happened to the courts post the Great Departure? Have they changed or rebranded? Destroyed outright?<br /> <br /> I would be interested to read through all of your thoughts and ideas!</div> </div> </div> </div>How did you handle the San Francisco situation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T02:24:42-07:00","id":1506219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1504195-kuei-jin-the-hungry-ghost?p=1506211#post1506211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How did you handle the San Francisco situation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Following the V5 Canon, The New Promise Mandarinate has disappeared following the Great Departure, with similar situation as it did in Chicago and all other US cities.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27804-studiokohvi","name":"Studiokohvi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27804_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T04:11:23-07:00","id":1506223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Studiokohvi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1504195-kuei-jin-the-hungry-ghost?p=1505012#post1505012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Does this matter though? Not to be a dick, but WOD isn't a good source of Any of the cultural influences it steals from.<br /> <br /> For europe alone: The vampire books absolutely manhandles european politics and hisory, with it placing &quot;major centers&quot; in middle-of-nowhere cities with populations too low to sustain any vampires, uses confused and misrepresented takes on european mythology to make cool powers for its magic system, and often disreprects the historical accomplishments of humanity by rewriting them as supernaturals.<br /> <br /> We accept that though because VTM isn't about europe, it's a love letter to a specific anne rice style of vampire and cheesy 90's horror movies. That's why there's often a list of book and movie references in the first chapter of every WOD book.<br /> <br /> KOTE is the same way, it's a world based entirely on cheesy martial arts movies and anime, Not the IRL cultures of asia.<br /> <br /> The game is a time capsule for the perspective american in the 90's, not some insightful look into the mythology and culrure of the world(though the game can sometimes have that too).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T06:43:53-07:00","id":1506230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1504195-kuei-jin-the-hungry-ghost?p=1506223#post1506223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does this matter though? Not to be a dick, but WOD isn't a good source of Any of the cultural influences it steals from.<br /> <br /> For europe alone: The vampire books absolutely manhandles european politics and hisory, with it placing &quot;major centers&quot; in middle-of-nowhere cities with populations too low to sustain any vampires, uses confused and misrepresented takes on european mythology to make cool powers for its magic system, and often disreprects the historical accomplishments of humanity by rewriting them as supernaturals.<br /> <br /> We accept that though because VTM isn't about europe, it's a love letter to a specific anne rice style of vampire and cheesy 90's horror movies. That's why there's often a list of book and movie references in the first chapter of every WOD book.<br /> <br /> KOTE is the same way, it's a world based entirely on cheesy martial arts movies and anime, Not the IRL cultures of asia.<br /> <br /> The game is a time capsule for the perspective american in the 90's, not some insightful look into the mythology and culrure of the world(though the game can sometimes have that too).</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct in that the books itself is very clearly written from an US standpoint.<br /> <br /> However the counterpoint I can say is that the WoD is very clearly our world but \u2018Darker\u2019 and has been since the inception of its universe. The metaplot uses wod creatures as you have said as the main reason why certain human decisions or achievements have been done which is done globally. IMO that still doesn\u2019t give it a pass on making cultural misunderstandings as when reading through old WoD, its very clear (aside from possibly DtF) that the creatures and beliefs are also shaped by the human society they have to hide behind. This in a sense requires a creature to mingle and understand the people they are pretending as or possibly what they believe in.<br /> <br /> As such, ultimately when roleplaying these creatures we\u2019re going to be picking up what our characters went through, how they perceive things and what cultural understandings they have been exposed to and base their viewpoint on.<br /> <br /> The thing about VTM in lets say Europe is that even though its a \u2018western\u2019 culture, the fact that the errors portrayed does cause gripes in Europeans and thats why there are lots of fan sites who try to translate VTM into parts of their country to make it more accurate and also try to stop using their languages as exotic in its lexicon (an example in vtm is papillon and butterfly. Papillon is french for butterfly but in vtm context means red light district whilst the term butterfly in vtm means someone who mingles in high society. Does that mean French vampires swap these terms and say Butterfly in their vocab or suddenly english is the native default for vamps?)<br /> <br /> Whilst I definitely don\u2019t speak for everyone, from my experience, there are a decent portion of people who don\u2019t go beyond the stereotype of who they characterise because they aren\u2019t aware. If someone is aware but plays the stereotype ironically, then thats fair enough. However, too often you get a response of \u2018wait, that isint normally how they talk/ think etc?\u2019.<br /> <br /> As such, some of the first exposures of different cultures could be through WoD. Some people will be interested and research deeper whilst a fair amount will take what is written at face value. In this case, better to have a more accurate understanding as your first basis over stereotypes. Building on your point, isint it better to have games that are fun but also insightful on other cultures and their mythology?<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27804-studiokohvi","name":"Studiokohvi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27804_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T09:05:06-07:00","id":1506237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Studiokohvi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1504195-kuei-jin-the-hungry-ghost?p=1506230#post1506230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Building on your point, isint it better to have games that are fun but also insightful on other cultures and their mythology?<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>In an ideal world? Sure.<br /> Do I think that's realistic? No.<br /> <br /> Let's remember we are talking about a niche roleplaying game that for all it's text about &quot;our world, but darker&quot; still takes place in a fantasy world where the authors took creative liberties for a specific purpose in each game.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's fair to criticize a the game for not being accurate to reality when it wasn't intended as an accurate depiction of reality to begin with. It'd be a nice bonus, but that'd be secondary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T17:26:00-07:00","id":1506275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Studiokohvi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1504195-kuei-jin-the-hungry-ghost?p=1506219#post1506219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Following the V5 Canon, The New Promise Mandarinate has disappeared following the Great Departure, with similar situation as it did in Chicago and all other US cities.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of the issue isn't it as V5 completely removed them entirely. At minimum the HG now have no noteworthy presence in North America and no longer control Tokyo. So really it would force us to keep them in Eastern Asia only which kind of flies in the face of the removal of the notion that only people from that particular region become HG because what's the point in having that if Eastern Asia is the only place where the HG have any kind of real presence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T14:29:21-07:00","id":1506363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1504195-kuei-jin-the-hungry-ghost?p=1506237#post1506237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In an ideal world? Sure.<br /> Do I think that's realistic? No.<br /> <br /> Let's remember we are talking about a niche roleplaying game that for all it's text about &quot;our world, but darker&quot; still takes place in a fantasy world where the authors took creative liberties for a specific purpose in each game.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's fair to criticize a the game for not being accurate to reality when it wasn't intended as an accurate depiction of reality to begin with. It'd be a nice bonus, but that'd be secondary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand where you are coming from and it is a valid statement. I am idealistic by nature so my stance is based around that it can be done which has been by approach towards it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27804-studiokohvi","name":"Studiokohvi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27804_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T14:41:07-07:00","id":1506365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1504195-kuei-jin-the-hungry-ghost?p=1506275#post1506275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's kind of the issue isn't it as V5 completely removed them entirely. At minimum the HG now have no noteworthy presence in North America and no longer control Tokyo. So really it would force us to keep them in Eastern Asia only which kind of flies in the face of the removal of the notion that only people from that particular region become HG because what's the point in having that if Eastern Asia is the only place where the HG have any kind of real presence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hello Akatsuki,<br /> Again thank you for your review. It meant a lot to me for your thoughts.<br /> <br /> In my own game set in London, after the Great Departure in 2004, a Preceptor arrived to London in 2008. During that time the game was set in 2019 meaning 11 years have allowed the Preceptor to rebuild their population, albeit less than in the past. However, because there is no restriction in ethnicity, there is a lot more HG that can arise hence my reasoning in being built up. Any news the camarilla or anarch hear about a wight, the preceptor will also look out for. In turn, once there is a sustainable population, a new court was declared known as the Court of Lions Flames in 2019.<br /> <br /> What was done with my thoughts was that since 2004, up to 80% of the population vanished. However that doesnt mean that some population wont come back. There is an eeriness especially if a HG follows the doctrine of the moon in which they will pass off as a vampire rather than a HG meaning a camarilla or anarch state can be harbouring a court in the making, biding their time. This to me is that whilst all the old courts established outside of Asia has disappeared, there is now infinite potential in how you want and explain how courts are made, like what I did with my own game. The difference is now the HG in a lot of areas are no longer a dominant faction, they are in their survival state or creation stage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27804-studiokohvi","name":"Studiokohvi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27804_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T21:52:17-07:00","id":1506403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Studiokohvi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1504195-kuei-jin-the-hungry-ghost?p=1506365#post1506365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hello Akatsuki,<br /> Again thank you for your review. It meant a lot to me for your thoughts.<br /> <br /> In my own game set in London, after the Great Departure in 2004, a Preceptor arrived to London in 2008. During that time the game was set in 2019 meaning 11 years have allowed the Preceptor to rebuild their population, albeit less than in the past. However, because there is no restriction in ethnicity, there is a lot more HG that can arise hence my reasoning in being built up. Any news the camarilla or anarch hear about a wight, the preceptor will also look out for. In turn, once there is a sustainable population, a new court was declared known as the Court of Lions Flames in 2019.<br /> <br /> What was done with my thoughts was that since 2004, up to 80% of the population vanished. However that doesnt mean that some population wont come back. There is an eeriness especially if a HG follows the doctrine of the moon in which they will pass off as a vampire rather than a HG meaning a camarilla or anarch state can be harbouring a court in the making, biding their time. This to me is that whilst all the old courts established outside of Asia has disappeared, there is now infinite potential in how you want and explain how courts are made, like what I did with my own game. The difference is now the HG in a lot of areas are no longer a dominant faction, they are in their survival state or creation stage.</div> </div> </div> </div>And as I said in my review, while I understand why you did the Great Departure, I don't like it and this is one of the reasons why. Because you're put us in a situation where unless we're playing in India and Eastern Asia (and even then given V5's stance on KotE, not really even there) we're stuck playing on the fringes of cities, hiding in the shadows of the Camarilla, Anarchs and even in a few cities, the Hecata. Sure that can be fine for some games but after a while it kind of gets tiresome. There are times when we want to play in HG Courts that have real power within their cities. Sure, they had time to rebuild but at the same time Cainites will fill the vacuum and take up the reigns of power, leaving the HG politically insignificant. Not to mention between the Embrace and creating Ghouls, the Cainities once entrenched will be very hard to remove. And after the invasion of the Anarch Free State, it's unlikely that most Princes or Baron are likely to be happy about HG popping up in their cities. Especially on the America West Coast. Or for that matter India given their history.<br /> <br /> It also kind of makes much of the Scarlet Screens pointless as if they have little local control there's little reason to control local mortal organizations.<br /> <br /> In my review I mentioned how some of the things in the book are in line with my own ideas and ones I've used in the few V20 games I've run over the years. A number of them revolving around the former New Promise Mandarinate as my games were all set in North America.<br /> <br /> In my games the NPM was never really intended by the Ancestors to actually succeed more than a few years. It's true purpose was to do two things, scare off the encroaching Cainites and get rid of troublesome HG, namely those that are young rebellious types and those seeking change and reform in the Courts. It was only a partial success. Initially the invasion was actually more successful than they had excepted however due to all the 'trouble-makers' the NPM Courts grew increasingly out of their control. Especially when they began to discover that those born outside of their homelands could become HG, something most younger HG had no idea about and for those that were already more Western-looking it was a final straw. Because if Westerners could become HG like them, were the Ten Thousand Immortals truly of the Middle Kingdoms and the regions on it's periphery? And if the Quincunx was wrong or willing to lie about that, what else were they wrong/willing to lie about?<br /> <br /> Rather ironically I had it around 2004/2005 that the NPM Courts formally went from a pseudo-colony to an independent network of Courts known as the New Dawn Courts (I am terrible at coming up with names) across the North American West Coast. Of course it left them without any significant support from their homelands (indeed some of the elder HG in the NPM had fled or been destroyed during this event) while the Anarchs were bouncing back and looking to take back lost territory as the Cam sought to exploit the situation to their own ends. Leading to several years of bloody and largely inconclusive fighting.<br /> <br /> The NDC would eventually reach out to the Cam through the Giovanni and strike a deal with them. In exchange for seceding control over some of the cities they still held at that point and staying out of Cainite (or really Camarilla) affairs, the NDC would be permitted to establish Courts within Cam Cities and likewise be left alone by local Cam Authorities. Essentially a situation akin to the peace with the Giovanni as neither side was entirely sure if they could keep up the fighting without potentially breaking the Masquerade. Though the NDC was in a much worse state than they were letting on. For their part, the Anarchs didn't like the peace but couldn't do a whole lot about it.<br /> <br /> Since then the NDC has created a bit of a facade around themselves, projecting more strength than they actually have to keep the Cainities from attempting to restart the conflict and to protect their greatest secret, that non-Asians can become HG. Though they have also been using the latter to place agents among the local Cam and Anarchs. Even had in the last game I ran a group of HG setting up a Scarlet Screen of a New Age Eastern Philosophy group/pseudo-cult seemingly led by a black Caitiff that was basically being fed watered down versions of HG beliefs and philosophy that pretty much fooled my players, thinking them as just some harmless weirdos led by an equally weird and harmless ex-Shovelhead with a love of Eastern Philosophy and Mysticism. Though that was probably more because they knew little of substance about KotE and that said group and their secret HG masters weren't the primary antagonists.<br /> <br /> Honestly it's along those lines that I'm looking to for my upcoming game as I intend to set it in the West Coast. Partly because as you can tell I've played around with the old NPM for some time and partly because my players are only really familiar with KotE via VtMB. And like I've said I don't like the Great Departure and if I had to use it, I wouldn't have it anywhere near as bad as in the book. I want the HG to have a real presence and power in the West Coast, removing them and then trying to have them claw their way back in again isn't going to work with that.<br /> <br /> Frankly given what V5 has already taken away from them and will likely take from them in the future if there are any more mentions of Asia or India, the Great Departure only makes it sting all the more. I know I keep harping on this but I just really don't want the HG to be little more than scattered cults pretending to be courts attempting to reach a fraction of what they once had and are unlikely to ever achieve more than that fraction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-08T17:56:09-07:00","id":1507807,"title":"","content":"Been doing some brainstorming for positions within the HG Courts. The names are subject to change as this early draft stuff.<br /> <br /> Ancestor: The Prince analogue. Nothing much that needs to be said that isn't already in the core book.<br /> <br /> Council of Preceptors: The Primogen analogue. Advisors to the Ancestor on all manner of things from political or spiritual. Made up of the eldest of the local HG. The number can vary between courts. The more orthodox courts will seat only those of the Major Paths while others will seat a member for every Path present in the court. Smaller courts will have less simply because they don't have enough Preceptors to sit on the council. Regardless it is seen as improper for their to be more than one Preceptor for each Path on a Council.<br /> <br /> In smaller courts the Councilors might also possess other positions within the court and in the case of the Warden and Instructor, it's preferred that the roles are handled by those Preceptor rank due to their importance.<br /> <br /> Grave Warden: Responsible for monitoring graveyards and local body dumping sites for HG taking their Second Breath. They virtually always have a coterie under them to assist them in capturing the Ravenous Devils that rise. Even if the HG are just beginning to establish themselves in a city, the Warden will have a coterie from another city assigned to them until the local population has reached a level where they can have their own.<br /> <br /> Devil Instructor: Responsible for breaking the Ravenous Devils from their mindless state and beginning their instruction in the Ways of the HG or destroying them if they are unable to regain their minds. In smaller courts this might be the same HG as the Warden though most prefer to keep the roles separate so they can maximize their efforts. The Instructor might also have a coterie under them (often made up of Devil-Tigers) but not always.<br /> <br /> Master of Ceremonies: The HG analogue to the Keeper of Elysium and filling a similar role though they will actual officiate ceremonies within the court, especially those courts of a more spiritual bent.<br /> <br /> The Guardian: Akin to the Sheriff and Scourge, tasked with maintaining and protecting the local HG territory as well as hunting and destroying wayward HG sentenced to death. Like the Warden they will have a dedicated coterie to assist them in their tasks.<br /> <br /> The Monitor: A position that only exists within cities with a Cainite population as their role is to monitor the local Cainite population. This can be done by mundane or magical means. Unlike the other positions, there can be multiple Monitors in the court. There is also in some courts within Cainite a sub-group of Monitor some times mockingly referred to as the Eyes of Zao-Lat/Saulot where HG of non-Asian/Indian descendant pose as Cainites to infiltrate local Cainite groups as very few Cainites are aware that non-Asians and Indians can become HG.<br /> <br /> I have a few other position ideas including one that defends and maintains Nodes within the court's territory but they're in the initial phase at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T08:51:53-07:00","id":1508038,"title":"","content":"Wow thats fantastic stuff that! Funny enough was listening to the podcast review of Kuei Jin:The Hungry Ghost and the Devil Instructor role was named the \u2018Iron Mother\u2019. Honestly some really cool stuff and ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27804-studiokohvi","name":"Studiokohvi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27804_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T09:13:32-07:00","id":1510494,"title":"","content":"Hello everyone,<br /> <br /> It has now been a few months now since the release of the Kj: Hungry Ghost. It has been interesting reading through and assessing what people want more in the future. Valid criticisms are taken on board which seemingly had been mainly on lore, examples on how to run games and how to build courts (which Akutsuki has kindly contributed to their awesome input and ideas). This will be indeed be done in the expansion for the KJ: The Hungry Ghosts.<br /> <br /> Keeping this in mind, how has people\u2019s experience been running the HG within their games be it as PC characters or NPC\u2019s? Any stories that has arose out of it will be amazing!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27804-studiokohvi","name":"Studiokohvi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27804_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T10:33:40-07:00","id":1510496,"title":"","content":"I wonder if you gonna use or mention <b>Carpenter's Prophecy </b>from <b>HTR: The Walking Dead </b><br /> <br /> In life, he was Dennis &quot;The Carpenter&quot; Maxwell, small-time hood for the Chicago mob. Near the end of his afterlife, he became Carpenter169, one of the most controversial posters on hunter-net.org.<br /> He earned his nickname working for the Sforza famiglia, from his favorite tongue-loosening technique: nailing people's hands to tables. Ultimately, he was sold out by his girlfriend, the don's daughter Annabelle, and shot down right in front of her. His death didn't even make the front page.<br /> In death, he learned the ins and outs of life as one of the Restless Dead, and also learned of his girlfriend's connection to the Giovanni clan of vampires.<br /> In 1999, Maxwell was one of the wraiths blasted through the Shroud by the Sixth Great Maelstrom. Like a lot of them, he found himself involuntarily possessing a host body. Unlike most of them, he soon found the Heralds directing him to hunter-net.<br /> Long story short, Immediately prior to returning to the underworld, Maxwell (posting as Carpenter169) issued a prophecy on hunter-net. Originally articulated in several languages such as Latin, Portuguese, Italian, and German, bookworm55 (Jackson &quot;Jake&quot; Washington,) translated it as:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;The hour of flame comes and the Emporer of Hell manifests.<br /> The twin-souled children of Jade have risen from their graves and await the hour that will sweep aawy those whose souls are not divided.<br /> The storm heralds the hour of destruction and its winds shall fan the flames even higher. Heaven's step children wander, blind into the kindgdom of death, but their sight is keen.<br /> Rotten blood and rotten souls gather under the horns of blood.<br /> Fire shall not cleanse us, and our bones will be as sand.&quot;\u200b<br /> \u200b</i><br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T16:36:29-07:00","id":1510528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Studiokohvi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1504195-kuei-jin-the-hungry-ghost?p=1510494#post1510494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everyone,<br /> <br /> It has now been a few months now since the release of the Kj: Hungry Ghost. It has been interesting reading through and assessing what people want more in the future. Valid criticisms are taken on board which seemingly had been mainly on lore, examples on how to run games and how to build courts (which Akutsuki has kindly contributed to their awesome input and ideas). This will be indeed be done in the expansion for the KJ: The Hungry Ghosts.<br /> <br /> Keeping this in mind, how has people\u2019s experience been running the HG within their games be it as PC characters or NPC\u2019s? Any stories that has arose out of it will be amazing!</div> </div> </div> </div>I have bits and pieces as like I said I'm preparing to run a game in a month and half, two months from now. I've been slowly refreshing myself on KotE and going through some of my own old ideas from V20.<br /> <br /> I've talked about bit my concept of the New Dawn Courts as my game is going to be set in California, likely LA, mostly because the bulk of my players' experience with KotE is VtMB1 so probably best to keep them around something more familiar with. In fact I have thought about the PC all dying and taking their Second Breath during the events of the game. So pretty much all my ideas at the moment are centered on the North American West Coast.<br /> <br /> Oh and one thing I should have mentioned about my previous post about the various positions was that I intentionally went with fairly neutral titles like with the terms in the book itself were neutral with some having more elaborate or region specific alternate names.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1504195-kuei-jin-the-hungry-ghost?p=1510496#post1510496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if you gonna use or mention <b>Carpenter's Prophecy </b>from <b>HTR: The Walking Dead </b><br /> <br /> In life, he was Dennis &quot;The Carpenter&quot; Maxwell, small-time hood for the Chicago mob. Near the end of his afterlife, he became Carpenter169, one of the most controversial posters on hunter-net.org.<br /> He earned his nickname working for the Sforza famiglia, from his favorite tongue-loosening technique: nailing people's hands to tables. Ultimately, he was sold out by his girlfriend, the don's daughter Annabelle, and shot down right in front of her. His death didn't even make the front page.<br /> In death, he learned the ins and outs of life as one of the Restless Dead, and also learned of his girlfriend's connection to the Giovanni clan of vampires.<br /> In 1999, Maxwell was one of the wraiths blasted through the Shroud by the Sixth Great Maelstrom. Like a lot of them, he found himself involuntarily possessing a host body. Unlike most of them, he soon found the Heralds directing him to hunter-net.<br /> Long story short, Immediately prior to returning to the underworld, Maxwell (posting as Carpenter169) issued a prophecy on hunter-net. Originally articulated in several languages such as Latin, Portuguese, Italian, and German, bookworm55 (Jackson &quot;Jake&quot; Washington,) translated it as:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;The hour of flame comes and the Emporer of Hell manifests.<br /> The twin-souled children of Jade have risen from their graves and await the hour that will sweep aawy those whose souls are not divided.<br /> The storm heralds the hour of destruction and its winds shall fan the flames even higher. Heaven's step children wander, blind into the kindgdom of death, but their sight is keen.<br /> Rotten blood and rotten souls gather under the horns of blood.<br /> Fire shall not cleanse us, and our bones will be as sand.&quot;\u200b<br /> \u200b</i><br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually he just experienced a Harrowing due to the death of Annabelle and ended up back in the Skinlands afterwards due to the whole Shroud becoming the Stormwall. Even got tangled up in some events involving the Mummies of MtR.<br /> <br /> As for the prophecy, I'm on the fence about that because it's all part of the march to the Time of Judgement which didn't happen in V5 obviously. Especially with how H5 tosses out the Imbued.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T06:28:07-07:00","id":1512112,"title":"","content":"Yeah that sounds quite cool with your game! The New Dawn courts and how you personally updated in your game is interesting and personally would like an update with how your players react.<br /> <br /> In terms of using previous lore before the Wod 5 updates, generally going to be avoiding things that denote the end of the world directly (time of judgement era books) as its established non canon. My main focus on meta plot will be derived from old KoTe perspective but if there is anything interesting, please send it my way! Compared to a lot of you, my knowledge can be considered basic \ud83d\ude05<br /> <br /> As an update (subject to change), Im focusing on the courts so far (names subject to change) with each culture having their own unique forms of courts. Just as a teaser (names subject to change), Ill give the updated names. If you think there are better names for them due to cultural significance, please let me know!<br /> <br /> \u2022Clans of the Sun (Former name: Uji- Japan)<br /> \u2022Scions of the Three Seals (Former name: Green courts - Korea)<br /> \u2022The Golden Concordant (Former name: Golden Courts - SEA)<br /> \u2022Alliance of the Three Infinities (Former name: Infinite Thunder Courts - India)<br /> \u2022 League of the Five Phases (Former name: Quincunx - China)<br /> <br /> Courts that are rebuilding outside of Asia I will be denoting as \u2018Descendants\u2019 with each Descendent court having the framework and naming convention based on which Preceptor originally came from to start with. <br /> <br /> If there are any area of Asia you feel I should create a brand new court to base it on, don\u2019t hesitate to tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27804,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27804-studiokohvi","user":"Studiokohvi","date":".  Misspelled and addition 05-19-2023, 09:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27804-studiokohvi","name":"Studiokohvi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27804_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T20:33:14-07:00","id":1512814,"title":"","content":"Truthfully I wouldn't say I'm an expert on KotE. In fact I've not even read the entire line. In fact the only KotE books I've read either either entirely or mostly are Rulebook, the Companion, the Dharma Books, Blood and Silk, and the 1000 Hells. Everything else I've either read a few sections, skimmed through them or haven't touched. And even then what I have read, I read years ago. I've been going back to the material lately when I'm able to for my upcoming game, with San Francisco by Night being the next one on my stack as it had a chapter on the major players of the NPM back in the day to serve as inspiration for the history and politics of the NDC as when I used it in V20 games, it was always being viewed from an outside perspective so I didn't really develop much of the history and politics of the Courts because the players were always Cainites and largely outsiders with no real understanding of their politics.<br /> <br /> As for areas of Asia, I don't really have anything for that. That's one of the other reasons why I'm sticking to North America as my knowledge of Asia is rather limited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}